[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
Failures occur when action preconditions are assumed rather than verified. Before searching, confirm the target object exists in the scene or use a valid alternative label. Before picking, navigate close enough to the object and confirm proximity. After picking, only proceed if the pick action succeeded and the object is actually held. Before placing, confirm the robot is holding the object; otherwise pick it first. General principle: verify object existence, proximity, and held state before acting, and adapt to available alternatives instead of assuming a named object is present.

## Preliminary Thinking
1. Explore the scene and identify bread, a toaster, and a plate, or valid alternatives if exact labels are unavailable. 2. Navigate to the bread and pick it up only when within reach; verify the pick succeeded and the bread is held. 3. Navigate to the toaster and place the bread in it only while holding it; activate the toaster and wait for toast. 4. Navigate to the toaster and pick up the toast only when close enough; verify it is held. 5. Navigate to the plate and place the toast on the plate only while holding it; verify the toast is served on the plate. If any precondition fails, re-check object existence/labels, reposition or navigate closer, and retry with valid alternatives.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]